    authorOrRuler: 'Adolf Hitler',
    authorTitle: 'Führer and Reich Chancellor',
    year: 1939,
    yearDisplay: 'September 19, 1939',
    era: '20th Century',
    category: 'Monumental Speeches',
    civilization: 'Nazi Germany (Blitzkrieg Triumph Propaganda Study)',
    location: 'Artushof, Danzig (Gdańsk), Poland / Germany',
    originalLanguage: 'German',
    mediumOrFormat: 'Public Victory Address and Radio Broadcast',
    currentPreservationLocation: 'Bundesarchiv, Berlin / Deutsches Rundfunkarchiv',
    famousQuote: 'Poland will never rise again in the form of the Versailles Treaty. This is guaranteed not only by Germany, but also by Russia.',
    summary: 'HISTORICAL STUDY OF TRIUMPHALIST ANNEXATION: Following the rapid collapse of Polish resistance and the Soviet invasion of eastern Poland, Hitler travels to Danzig, gloating over the eradication of the Polish state and warning Britain and France that resistance to German hegemony is futile.',
    historicalContext: 'Delivered as German and Soviet forces linked up across partitioned Poland under the secret protocols of the Molotov-Ribbentrop Pact, initiating six years of brutal dual occupation.',
    fullExcerptText: `Danzig war deutsch, ist deutsch geblieben und wird von jetzt ab deutsch sein, solange es ein deutsches Volk und ein Deutsches Reich gibt!... Dieses Polen wird in der Gestalt des Versailler Vertrages niemals mehr erstehen! Dafür bürgt nicht nur Deutschland, dafür bürgt nunmehr auch Russland!... Wenn England aber glaubt, diesen Krieg bis zum Äußersten führen zu müssen, so wird Deutschland die Antwort darauf zu geben wissen...
    
(Historical Translation for Educational Study: Danzig was German, has remained German, and will from now on be German as long as there is a German nation and a German Reich!... This Poland will never again rise in the form of the Versailles Treaty! For this not only Germany guarantees, but now Russia also guarantees!... But if England believes it must wage this war to the bitter end, Germany will know how to give the answer...)`,
    keyClauses: [
      {
        clauseNumberOrTitle: 'Total Eradication of Polish Sovereignty',
        originalExcerpt: 'Dieses Polen wird in der Gestalt des Versailler Vertrages niemals mehr erstehen!',
        modernizedMeaning: 'Attempting to erase a sovereign nation permanently from the map through military conquest.',
        historicalSignificance: 'Marked the beginning of Generalplan Ost, resulting in the murder of six million Polish citizens, including three million Polish Jews.'
      }
    ],
    lastingImpact: 'Demonstrated the immediate partition of Eastern Europe between the Nazi and Soviet totalitarian regimes in September 1939.',
    audioSpeechText: 'Archival Educational Exhibit. September 19, 1939, in the Artushof of Danzig. Following the blitzkrieg collapse of Poland, Hitler celebrated the annexation of the city and declared that Poland would never rise again. Historians examine this address to document the ruthless dismantlement of Eastern European sovereign states in 1939.'
