    lastingImpact: 'Launched the six-week campaign that shattered Western European military strategy and established Nazi dominion over continental Western Europe.',
    audioSpeechText: 'Archival Educational Exhibit. May 10, 1940. Hitler’s supreme order of the day to the Wehrmacht troops launching the invasion of France, Belgium, and the Netherlands. This Blitzkrieg attack through the Ardennes surprised Allied generals, rapidly knocking France out of the war and reshaping twentieth-century history.'
