    lastingImpact: 'Marked the beginning of the Blitz, strengthening British civilian resolve and contributing to Nazi Germany’s first major military defeat in WWII.',
    audioSpeechText: 'Archival Educational Recording. September 4, 1940, at the Berlin Sportpalast. Hitler announced the commencement of the Blitz, shouting his famous phrase that German bombers would raze British cities to the ground. This tactical shift from military airfields to civilian targets gave the Royal Air Force the respite needed to triumph in the Battle of Britain.'
